  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 112 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nOur area will have a continuation of hot and dry conditions with \nmostly clear skies, with the prevailing influence from a large and \nexpansive upper level ridge. This ridge will be centered over the \nlower Mississippi Valley on Saturday, then shift west over North \nTexas Sunday night into Monday, and then over New Mexico Tuesday \nthrough midweek. While little change is expected with daily low \ntemperatures, there are some indications that the 850mb thermal \nridge may strengthen over our area in the early to middle parts of \nnext week. This suggests an uptick in the daily highs, with most of \nour area at or above 100 degrees, and a larger part of the Big \nCountry and some of the Concho Valley pushing Heat Advisory \ncriteria. South winds will continue each day, but wind speeds should \nbe a little lower Sunday through Tuesday as the surface pressure \ngradient weakens to some extent.",
